    "## Network structure: diameter, efficiency, clustering, communities, bridges\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Diameter** and **average shortest path length** are only defined for a\n",
    "  connected graph, so they're computed on the *largest* connected component\n",
    "  when the network isn't fully connected.\n",
    "- **Global efficiency** measures how easily information (or, by analogy,\n",
    "  power) could reach across the whole network on average - closer to 1\n",
    "  means every pair of substations is close together; closer to 0 means\n",
    "  they're far apart or disconnected.\n",
    "- **Community detection** (greedy modularity) groups substations into\n",
    "  clusters that are more densely connected internally than to the rest of\n",
    "  the network - a structural proxy for \"regional clusters\".\n",
    "- **Bridges** are individual lines whose removal alone would split the\n",
    "  network into more pieces - single points of connection, distinct from\n",
    "  removing a whole substation (that's the N-1 test below)."
